{"title":"Career Roadmap — Polysomnography Technologist","role":"Polysomnography Technologist","summary":"A Polysomnography Technologist conducts and supports sleep studies used to evaluate sleep-related disorders. The technologist prepares patients, applies physiological sensors, operates polysomnography equipment, monitors recordings during sleep, identifies technical abnormalities and clinically significant events for appropriate escalation, and prepares high-quality study data for interpretation by qualified sleep physicians.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences — B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.","Course":"Sleep Technology / Endoscopy Technology"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Workplaces","text":"Sleep laboratories, hospitals, respiratory-care centres, neurology departments, pulmonology departments, sleep-medicine clinics, research centres"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Polysomnography Technologist conducts and supports sleep studies used to evaluate sleep-related disorders. The technologist prepares patients, applies physiological sensors, operates polysomnography equipment, monitors recordings during sleep, identifies technical abnormalities and clinically significant events for appropriate escalation, and prepares high-quality study data for interpretation by qualified sleep physicians."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation and education"},{"text":"Sensor/electrode placement"},{"text":"Polysomnography setup"},{"text":"Overnight physiological monitoring"},{"text":"ECG and respiratory monitoring"},{"text":"EEG/EOG/EMG recording"},{"text":"Pulse oximetry"},{"text":"Event annotation"},{"text":"CPAP/BiPAP titration support where authorized"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"},{"text":"Sleep-study documentation"},{"text":"Data quality control"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist does not independently diagnose sleep disorders. Final diagnosis and clinical interpretation are performed by appropriately qualified physicians/sleep specialists."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Horizon 1 — Entry-Level Sleep Technologist"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polysomnography Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Lab Technician"},{"text":"Sleep Study Technician"},{"text":"Sleep Laboratory Technologist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Horizon 2 — Experienced Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Sleep Technologist"},{"text":"Senior Polysomnography Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Lab Supervisor"},{"text":"CPAP Titration Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Diagnostics Coordinator"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Horizon 3 — Advanced Operations"},{"type":"h","text":"5+ years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chief Sleep Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Laboratory Manager"},{"text":"Sleep Diagnostics Supervisor"},{"text":"Sleep Medicine Program Coordinator"},{"text":"Clinical Sleep Technology Specialist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Horizon 4 — Research / Advanced Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sleep Research Technologist"},{"text":"Sleep Data Analyst"},{"text":"Digital Sleep Monitoring Specialist"},{"text":"Sleep Technology Application Specialist"},{"text":"Clinical Research Coordinator"}]}]},{"heading":"UG Roadmap — Year 1","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Build Biomedical Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Human Anatomy"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain and nervous system"},{"text":"Respiratory system"},{"text":"Cardiovascular system"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal system"},{"text":"Upper airway anatomy"},{"text":"Thoracic anatomy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human Physiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respiratory physiology"},{"text":"Cardiovascular physiology"},{"text":"Neural regulation"},{"text":"Muscle physiology"},{"text":"Oxygen transport"},{"text":"Gas exchange"},{"text":"Autonomic nervous system"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurophysiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain activity"},{"text":"Neurons"},{"text":"EEG principles"},{"text":"Sleep-wake regulation"},{"text":"Circadian rhythms"},{"text":"Brain-wave patterns"}]}]},{"heading":"Sleep Science Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the basic architecture of sleep."},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Stages"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wakefulness"},{"text":"NREM sleep"},{"text":"N1"},{"text":"N2"},{"text":"N3"},{"text":"REM sleep"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the physiological characteristics associated with each stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Circadian Biology"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Circadian rhythm"},{"text":"Biological clock"},{"text":"Melatonin"},{"text":"Sleep-wake cycle"},{"text":"Light exposure"},{"text":"Shift-work effects"},{"text":"Jet lag"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Regulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Homeostatic sleep drive"},{"text":"Circadian sleep drive"},{"text":"Sleep pressure"},{"text":"Sleep deprivation"}]}]},{"heading":"UG Roadmap — Year 2","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Polysomnography Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the components of a standard sleep study."},{"type":"h","text":"EEG"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG electrode placement concepts"},{"text":"Brain-wave recording"},{"text":"Signal quality"},{"text":"Artifacts"},{"text":"Basic waveform recognition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"EOG"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Eye movements"},{"text":"EOG channels"},{"text":"REM identification"},{"text":"Signal artifacts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"EMG"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chin EMG"},{"text":"Leg EMG"},{"text":"Muscle activity"},{"text":"Periodic limb movement monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ECG"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG electrode placement"},{"text":"Heart-rate monitoring"},{"text":"Rhythm observation"},{"text":"Basic artifact recognition"}]}]},{"heading":"Respiratory Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a core component of sleep studies."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airflow monitoring"},{"text":"Respiratory effort"},{"text":"Thoracic movement"},{"text":"Abdominal movement"},{"text":"Respiratory belts"},{"text":"Nasal pressure"},{"text":"Oxygen saturation"},{"text":"Pulse rate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how respiratory signals help identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Apnea"},{"text":"Hypopnea"},{"text":"Oxygen desaturation"},{"text":"Respiratory effort abnormalities"}]}]},{"heading":"UG Roadmap — Year 3","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Conduct Complete Sleep Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient preparation","History","Equipment setup","Sensor application","Calibration","Recording","Overnight monitoring","Event annotation","Quality review","Report preparation","Physician interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Explaining the procedure"},{"text":"Obtaining appropriate consent according to institutional procedures"},{"text":"Preparing the sleep environment"},{"text":"Applying sensors comfortably"},{"text":"Addressing patient concerns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical Calibration"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Signal calibration"},{"text":"Bio-signal verification"},{"text":"Impedance checks"},{"text":"Sensor troubleshooting"},{"text":"Baseline recording"},{"text":"Recording quality assessment"}]}]},{"heading":"Sleep Disorders — Foundational Knowledge","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A technologist should understand the basic characteristics of common sleep disorders."},{"type":"h","text":"Obstructive Sleep Apnea"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Upper-airway obstruction"},{"text":"Snoring"},{"text":"Apnea/hypopnea events"},{"text":"Oxygen desaturation"},{"text":"Respiratory effort"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Central Sleep Apnea"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reduced/absent respiratory effort"},{"text":"Central respiratory events"},{"text":"Relationship with underlying conditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Insomnia"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Difficulty initiating sleep"},{"text":"Difficulty maintaining sleep"},{"text":"Sleep-quality complaints"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Narcolepsy"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic concepts of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excessive daytime sleepiness"},{"text":"REM-related abnormalities"},{"text":"Cataplexy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Periodic Limb Movements"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Leg EMG monitoring"},{"text":"Periodic movements"},{"text":"Relationship with sleep disruption"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Parasomnias"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Abnormal behaviors during sleep"},{"text":"REM-related and NREM-related phenomena"}]}]},{"heading":"CPAP / PAP Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of positive-airway-pressure therapy."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CPAP"},{"text":"Auto-CPAP"},{"text":"BiPAP"},{"text":"PAP masks"},{"text":"Pressure settings"},{"text":"Mask fitting"},{"text":"Leak monitoring"},{"text":"Patient comfort"},{"text":"Titration principles"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Where permitted, gain supervised experience supporting PAP titration studies."},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist should follow the prescribing physician's orders and institutional protocols rather than independently prescribing or changing treatment."}]},{"heading":"Overnight Monitoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong real-time observation skills."},{"type":"p","text":"Monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"EOG"},{"text":"EMG"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Airflow"},{"text":"Respiratory effort"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"Body position"},{"text":"Snoring"},{"text":"Limb movements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During the Study"},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Identify poor-quality signals"},{"text":"Correct technical problems"},{"text":"Replace displaced sensors"},{"text":"Document significant events"},{"text":"Maintain patient safety"},{"text":"Escalate clinical concerns appropriately"}]}]},{"heading":"Sleep Study Data & Scoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles behind:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Architecture"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Total sleep time"},{"text":"Sleep efficiency"},{"text":"Sleep latency"},{"text":"REM latency"},{"text":"Sleep-stage distribution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Respiratory Metrics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Apnea-hypopnea index (AHI)"},{"text":"Respiratory event index"},{"text":"Oxygen desaturation"},{"text":"Oxygen saturation trends"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Metrics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the concepts of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arousal index"},{"text":"Periodic limb movement index"},{"text":"Heart-rate trends"},{"text":"Wake after sleep onset"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These metrics should be interpreted according to accepted scoring standards and under the appropriate clinical supervision."}]},{"heading":"Equipment & Troubleshooting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A good technologist must be technically strong."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to troubleshoot:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG signal loss"},{"text":"EOG signal problems"},{"text":"EMG artifacts"},{"text":"ECG interference"},{"text":"Poor airflow signals"},{"text":"Respiratory belt displacement"},{"text":"Oximeter problems"},{"text":"Electrode impedance issues"},{"text":"Electrical interference"},{"text":"Computer/software problems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PSG acquisition systems"},{"text":"Amplifiers"},{"text":"Electrodes"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"PAP devices"},{"text":"Pulse oximeters"},{"text":"ECG equipment"},{"text":"Sleep-lab computers"}]}]},{"heading":"Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Expected Competency"],"rows":[[{"text":"Sleep physiology"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Sleep staging fundamentals"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"EOG"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"EMG"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Respiratory monitoring"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Pulse oximetry"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Sensor placement"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"PSG setup"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Overnight monitoring"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Signal troubleshooting"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Sleep-study scoring"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"PAP technology"},{"text":"Intermediate–Strong"}],[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Digital data management"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Strong"}]]}]},{"heading":"Clinical Internship","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Clinical exposure is essential for this career."},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Internship Locations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sleep laboratories"},{"text":"Pulmonology departments"},{"text":"Neurology departments"},{"text":"Respiratory-care centres"},{"text":"Hospitals with sleep-medicine services"},{"text":"Dedicated sleep clinics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to gain experience with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"PSG setup"},{"text":"Electrode placement"},{"text":"Sensor calibration"},{"text":"Overnight monitoring"},{"text":"Sleep staging"},{"text":"Respiratory event identification"},{"text":"PAP titration"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"},{"text":"Sleep-study documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should perform clinical procedures only under authorized supervision and within their scope of practice."}]},{"heading":"Practical Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Complete PSG Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient","Preparation","Sensor Placement","Calibration","Overnight Recording","Scoring","Quality Review","Physician Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Sleep Signal Artifact Library"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an academic collection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG artifacts"},{"text":"ECG artifacts"},{"text":"Movement artifacts"},{"text":"Electrode artifacts"},{"text":"Respiratory signal artifacts"},{"text":"Oximetry artifacts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Explain how each can affect recording quality."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Sleep Study Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an Excel/Power BI dashboard containing anonymized study metrics such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Total sleep time"},{"text":"Sleep efficiency"},{"text":"AHI"},{"text":"Oxygen saturation"},{"text":"Sleep-stage percentages"},{"text":"PLM index"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — PAP Titration Case Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a simulated academic case demonstrating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Baseline respiratory events"},{"text":"PAP intervention"},{"text":"Pressure changes under a defined protocol"},{"text":"Changes in respiratory events"},{"text":"Oxygenation trends"}]}]},{"heading":"Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Filtering"},{"text":"Pivot tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Trend analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Sleep-lab databases"},{"text":"Patient identifiers"},{"text":"Data privacy"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Option"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Pandas"},{"text":"Signal processing fundamentals"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Basic machine learning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can open pathways into sleep research and digital health."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Training","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful training areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic Life Support (BLS)"},{"text":"First Aid"},{"text":"Sleep technology"},{"text":"Polysomnography"},{"text":"Sleep-study scoring"},{"text":"PAP/CPAP technology"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Healthcare quality management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International professional certifications may also be valuable where their eligibility requirements are met. Candidates should verify current requirements with the issuing organization before pursuing them."}]},{"heading":"Higher Education","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical / Allied Health"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Sleep Technology, where available"},{"text":"M.Sc. Respiratory Therapy"},{"text":"M.Sc. Allied Health Sciences"},{"text":"M.Sc. Neurophysiology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Medical Physiology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Management"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Master of Hospital Administration"},{"text":"MBA Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Master of Public Health"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neuroscience"},{"text":"Sleep Science"},{"text":"Respiratory Physiology"},{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Biomedical Sciences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility depends on the candidate's exact UG qualification and university requirements."}]},{"heading":"Specialization Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Apnea"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PSG"},{"text":"Respiratory monitoring"},{"text":"PAP titration"},{"text":"Sleep-disordered breathing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pediatric Sleep"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn specialized considerations for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Children"},{"text":"Pediatric sleep apnea"},{"text":"Developmental sleep patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neuro-Sleep"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"REM disorders"},{"text":"Narcolepsy"},{"text":"Neurological sleep disorders"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PAP Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CPAP"},{"text":"BiPAP"},{"text":"Mask fitting"},{"text":"Compliance monitoring"},{"text":"Patient education"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sleep datasets"},{"text":"Signal processing"},{"text":"Clinical studies"},{"text":"Sleep biomarkers"},{"text":"AI-assisted sleep analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A possible pathway:"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Sc. Allied Health / Sleep Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Polysomnography Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Sleep Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Laboratory Supervisor"},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Diagnostics / Program Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Laboratory Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Technology Specialist / Research Lead"}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI-Based Sleep Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automated sleep staging"},{"text":"Respiratory event detection"},{"text":"Snoring analysis"},{"text":"Sleep-pattern classification"},{"text":"Signal-quality monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Wearable Sleep Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Increasingly available technologies include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Smartwatches"},{"text":"Wearable oximeters"},{"text":"Home sleep testing devices"},{"text":"Portable respiratory monitors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Home Sleep Apnea Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Sleep diagnostics are increasingly moving beyond traditional overnight laboratories for appropriately selected patients."},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud-Based Sleep Platforms"},{"type":"p","text":"Can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Remote data transfer"},{"text":"Physician review"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"PAP adherence tracking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Signal Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced technologists can learn to analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"respiratory signals"},{"text":"SpO₂ time series"},{"text":"movement signals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates opportunities in digital health and sleep-tech companies."}]},{"heading":"Professional Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient empathy"},{"text":"Night-shift discipline"},{"text":"Attention to detail"},{"text":"Technical troubleshooting"},{"text":"Calm decision-making"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Clinical observation"},{"text":"Documentation accuracy"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Equipment handling"},{"text":"Safety awareness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Because sleep studies frequently occur overnight, the student should also be comfortable working independently for extended periods while maintaining continuous patient observation."}]},{"heading":"Ideal Student Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to:"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare patients for diagnostic sleep studies, correctly set up and monitor polysomnographic equipment, acquire high-quality EEG/EOG/EMG, ECG and respiratory signals, recognize sleep stages and major physiological events at a foundational level, troubleshoot technical problems, document overnight observations, support PAP titration where authorized, and maintain patient safety and data quality throughout the study."},{"type":"h","text":"Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sleep Physiology","Neurophysiology","PSG","EEG","EOG","EMG","ECG","Respiratory Monitoring","Sleep Staging","Sleep Scoring","PAP Technology","Patient Care","Signal Troubleshooting","Clinical Documentation","Digital Sleep Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Polysomnography expertise","respiratory monitoring","neurophysiology","PAP technology","digital sleep analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination positions the graduate for both hospital-based sleep laboratories and the growing digital sleep-health and remote-monitoring sector."}]}]}